  "question": {
    "text": "A particle moving in a circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> with uniform speed takes time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> to complete one revolution. If this particle is projected with the same speed at an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>θ</mi></math> to the horizontal, the maximum height attained by it is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>R</mi></math>. The angle of projection <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>θ</mi></math> is then given by :",
    "image": null
  },
